Attack 1 — error-path divergence (Clone vs DeepCopy): NOT EXPLOITABLE.
prepare.Clone (prepare.go:127-137) is literally `out, err := DeepCopy(cfg);
... carryJSONOmittedFields(cfg, out); return out, nil` — carryJSONOmittedFields
never errors, so Clone's error surface is byte-for-byte DeepCopy's. Probed a
NaN MonthlyLivingExpenses (json.Marshal-rejects) against both the new code and
a locally-reverted-to-DeepCopy copy of Apply: identical error
("marshal: json: unsupported value: NaN") both ways. No regression.

Attack 2 — behavior delta (CurrentAge/SpouseAge now survive Apply where
DeepCopy used to zero them): real semantic change to Apply's return value,
but traced every consumer and found none observes it today:
  - settings.go:1185 ApplyOverrides -> the returned `cloned` (Clone of Apply's
    output) is discarded by handlers_live.go:89 (`_, scenario, revision, err`)
  - register.go:236 apply_changes feeds the same `settings` through
    prepare.From(settings), which runs its OWN internal DeepCopy (dropping
